WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.640
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:11.520
Today we are going to look at NVIDIA’s spectacular&nbsp;
new AI that can generate beautiful images for us.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.240
But, this is not image generation of any kind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.960
no-no! This is different.&nbsp;
Let’s see how it is different.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:27.200
For instance, we can write a description,&nbsp;
and the appropriate image comes out. Snowy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:34.000
mountains, pink cloudy sky. Checkmark.
Okay, we can give it art direction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:42.240
Make no mistake, this is fantastic, but this&nbsp;
has been done before, nothing new here. Yet.&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:48.000
Or, we can create a segmentation map,&nbsp;
this tells the AI what things are.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.560
The sea is down there, mountains,&nbsp;
and sky up there. Looking great, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.760
this has been done before too. For&nbsp;
instance, NVIDIA’s previous GauGAN paper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:06.960
could do this too. Nothing new here. Yet.
Or, we can tell the AI where things are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:12.240
by sketching. This one also&nbsp;
works, but this has been done too.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:19.760
So, is there nothing new in this paper? Well, of&nbsp;
course there is! And now, hold on to your papers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:24.320
and watch as we fuse all of&nbsp;
these descriptions together.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:30.640
We tell it where things are and what&nbsp;
things are. But I wonder if we can make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:38.800
this mountain snowy and a pink cloudy sky&nbsp;
on top of all things….yes we can! Oh wow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:45.280
I love it. The sea could have a little more&nbsp;
detail, but the rest of the image is spectacular.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:50.240
So, with this new technique, we&nbsp;
can tell an AI where things are,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:55.840
what things are, and on top of it,&nbsp;
we can also give it art direction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.000
And here is the key, all of these&nbsp;
can be done, in any combination!

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:07.600
Now, did you see it? Curiously, an image&nbsp;
popped up at the start of the video when we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:14.240
unchecked all the boxes. Why is that? Is that&nbsp;
a bug? I’ll tell you in a bit what that is.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:21.760
So far, these were great examples, but let’s try&nbsp;
to push this to its limits and see what it can do.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:28.480
For instance, how quickly can we iterate with&nbsp;
it? How quick is it to correct mistakes or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:35.120
improve the work? Oh boy. Super quick!&nbsp;
When giving art direction to the AI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:40.800
we can update the text, and the output&nbsp;
refreshes almost as quickly as we can type.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:46.480
The sketch to image feature is also&nbsp;
a great tool by itself. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.120
there is not only one way to satisfy these labels,&nbsp;
there are many pictures that this could describe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:57.760
so, how do we control what we get? Well,&nbsp;
it can even generate variants for us.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.520
With this new work, we can even draw a&nbsp;
piece of rock within a within the sea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:10.080
and the rock will indeed appear. Not only&nbsp;
that, but it understands that the waves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:18.240
have to go around it too. An understanding&nbsp;
of physics. That is insanity. My goodness.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:24.960
Or, better, if we know in advance that we are&nbsp;
looking for tall trees and autumn leaves, we can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:31.600
start with the art direction. And then, when&nbsp;
we add our labels, they will be satisfied,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:40.000
we can have our river, but the trees and&nbsp;
the leaves will always be there. Finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:45.840
we can sketch on top of this to have&nbsp;
additional control over the hills and clouds.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:50.240
And, get this - we can even edit real images.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:57.840
So, how does this black magic work? Well, we&nbsp;
have four neural networks, four experts if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:05.840
will. And the new technique describes how to fuse&nbsp;
their expertise together into one amazing package.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:11.760
And the result is a technique that outperforms&nbsp;
previous techniques in most of the tested cases.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:19.520
So, are these some ancient methods from many&nbsp;
years ago that are outperformed, or are they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:25.360
cutting edge? And here comes the best part. If&nbsp;
you have been holding on to your papers so far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:30.560
now, squeeze that paper, because these&nbsp;
techniques are not some ancient methods.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:37.360
Not at all. Both of these methods are from the&nbsp;
same year as this technique. The same year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:44.880
Such improvement in less than a year. That&nbsp;
is outstanding. What a time to be alive!

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:51.200
Now, I made a promise to you early in the&nbsp;
video. And the promise is explaining this. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:56.800
the technique generates, even when&nbsp;
not given a lot of instruction. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:03.120
this was the early example when we unchecked all&nbsp;
the boxes. What quality images can we expect then?&nbsp;&nbsp;

